=== entry 49969656b7a9
kind: translation
rules: delegate, isolation
intent: Parallel writers on one branch are `delegate_task` calls with `isolation: "worktree"`, which copies only committed work. Preserves the worktree-off-main rule, the reset alternative, and the dirty and snarled worktree recoveries.
--- upstream
**Worktree.** Work from a git worktree off main. Subagents inherit it. Multiple `Task` calls on the same branch each get their own worktree, or `git fetch && git reset --hard origin/<branch>` between them. Dirty branch with unrelated work: patch out, fresh worktree, apply. Snarled worktree: reset from main, redo minimally.
--- patched
**Worktree.** Work from a git worktree off main. Subagents inherit it. Multiple `delegate_task` calls on the same branch each get their own worktree (`isolation: "worktree"`, a checkout of the parent's current local commit, so commit first), or `git fetch && git reset --hard origin/<branch>` between them. Dirty branch with unrelated work: patch out, fresh worktree, apply. Snarled worktree: reset from main, redo minimally.

=== entry 9a4d7f564f09
kind: translation
rules: team-kit, invoke
intent: `/deslop` loses its plugin name and runs only if installed. Preserves the order (deslop before commit, no-comments before review) and the technical-writing and unslop requirements. The deslop, no-comments, technical-writing, and unslop skills are named with no slash.
--- upstream
**PRs.** Run `/deslop` from `cursor-team-kit` over the diff before commit and `/no-comments` before review. Write every PR title, description, and commit body with `/technical-writing` (every layer except Diátaxis, and apply the STE vocabulary rules: one word per action, keep articles, a plain verb over `-ing` where one works), then apply `/unslop`.
--- patched
**PRs.** Run the **deslop** skill, if it is installed, over the diff before commit and the **no-comments** skill before review. Write every PR title, description, and commit body with the **technical-writing** skill (every layer except Diátaxis, and apply the STE vocabulary rules: one word per action, keep articles, a plain verb over `-ing` where one works), then apply the **unslop** skill.

=== entry f032890e6908
kind: translation
rules: invoke
intent: The subagent runs the deslop and no-comments skills, named with no slash. Preserve the no-babysitting default and the Autopilot owner exemption.
--- upstream
A subagent that opens a PR runs `/deslop` and `/no-comments`, and posts the URL. It returns to the parent without babysitting, unless it is an Autopilot-full or Autopilot-stack owner. That owner's brief assigns the babysit loop and is the ask `playbooks/babysit.md` waits for. The owner starts the loop after its code-ready report, reports merge-ready, and is exempt from the rules here and in `playbooks/babysit.md` that hold babysitting until a whole stack is built.
--- patched
A subagent that opens a PR runs the **deslop** and **no-comments** skills, and posts the URL. It returns to the parent without babysitting, unless it is an Autopilot-full or Autopilot-stack owner. That owner's brief assigns the babysit loop and is the ask `playbooks/babysit.md` waits for. The owner starts the loop after its code-ready report, reports merge-ready, and is exempt from the rules here and in `playbooks/babysit.md` that hold babysitting until a whole stack is built.
